From: tryinget <markus@team-wangler.de>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 02:03:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 07/13] test(e2e): cover readiness, frame.diagnose, extract and
 controlled inputs in real Chrome

Extend the pinned-Chrome E2E with fixture routes served by the same
throwaway server (plus a second server for a real cross-origin frame):

- page.readiness and wait.ready on the fixture page; wait.ready on a
  login page with --url-prefix fails with the login state and returns
  it with --accept login.
- frame.diagnose on a page with same-origin, srcdoc, cross-origin and
  sandboxed iframes: DOM/extension/CDP correlation, content-script
  PING, and the srcdoc / allow-scripts warnings.
- js --file with a statement script and --options (the CSP fallback).
- extract: rows with SURF_OPTIONS.limit, Markdown table, an explicit
  empty state accepted via --empty-text, the zero-rows invariant with
  two attempts, and no leaked owned tab.
- type --into on an input with a framework-style value tracker: the
  page's own input listener observes the typed value.

